  'export-artboards-pdf': ['File', 'Exports every artboard as one page of a single PDF, in the Layers order, each page at its artboard size from the document resolution; takes name, jpeg, quality and icc.', 'Use when the artboards are wanted together as one multipage PDF.', 'r'],
  'export-data-sets': ['File', 'Applies each data set in turn and exports the flattened document as [doc]_[dataset].png (or jpg, tiff, webp, psd by the format param; the template param names the files with {document}, {name} and {index}, repeated names are numbered), all in one zip; the document ends as it started.', 'Use to produce every variation of a template from imported data sets in one go.', 'r'],
  'measure-scale': ['Image', 'Sets the measurement scale: how many pixels make a logical length in chosen units. Without parameters it opens a dialog prefilled from the Ruler line.', 'Use when measurements must be reported in real units such as cm instead of pixels.', 'm'],
  'measure-data-points': ['Image', 'Chooses which measurements the Measurement Log and its CSV export show (label, scale, area, perimeter, length, angle, count, width, height, gray value and its minimum and maximum, integrated density, centroid, circularity).', 'Use when the log should show only some of the recorded values; recording still keeps every value.', ''],
  'measure-record-features': ['Image', 'Records one measurement for each separate part of the selection (area, perimeter, size, gray value, centroid), the Ruler line and the counts going on the first, scaled by the measurement scale.', 'Use when a selection holds several objects that each need their own row in the measurement log.', 'm'],
